  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Battery Storage for Grid-Resiliency Feasibility Study, through Det Norske Veritas Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study for Lekela Energie Stockage S.A.U., a privatelyowned company in Senegal, to fund a feasibility study (Study) to provide the technical, economic, and environmental analysis necessary to implement and operate a grid-scale battery electric storage system to manage variable renewable energy generation in Senegal (Project). The Project is anticipated to deploy at least 60 megawatt hours of grid-tied battery storage capacity. The Study would be competed among U.S. firms on the USTDA website and publicized via Sam.gov as well as highlighted through USTDA and Power Africa social media and marketing platforms</narrative>
  </description>
